        answer: "<div style='background-color: #f5f7fa; padding: 12px; border-left: 4px solid #2196f3; border-radius: 5px; font-size: 15px; color: #333;'><h4 style='color: #0d47a1; margin-top: 0;'>ઉકેલ:</h4><b>Devayani:</b><br>Devayani was the beautiful daughter of Shukracharya, the guru of the Asuras. She fell deeply in love with Kach, who was young, handsome, and intelligent. Whenever the Asuras killed Kach, she would cry and request her father to revive him. Because of her love, Shukracharya saved Kach's life three times. However, at the end of his training, Kach refused to marry her, saying that since he came out of her father's stomach, she was his sister. Out of anger and disappointment, Devayani cursed him that his Vidya would never be useful to him.<br><br><div style='background-color: #fff3e0; padding: 10px; margin-top: 15px; border-radius: 5px; border-left: 4px solid #ff9800; color: #e65100; font-weight: bold;'>🚀 નિતેશ સરની શોર્ટકટ ટ્રીક: દેવયાની માટે પોઇન્ટ્સ: 1. શુક્રાચાર્યની દીકરી, 2. કચના પ્રેમમાં પાગલ, 3. ત્રણ વાર પિતા પાસે કચને જીવતો કરાવ્યો, 4. કચે ના પાડી એટલે ગુસ્સામાં શ્રાપ આપ્યો!</div></div>"
